# Test: ze configured to SEND ADD-PATH negotiates it, because ze-peer answers
# the opposite direction rather than the same one.
#
# VALIDATES: RFC 7911 Section 4, whose Send/Receive field describes the SENDER.
#            ze-peer inverts each direction (invertedAddPath,
#            internal/test/peer/open.go), so Negotiate
#            (internal/core/bgp/capability/negotiated.go) intersects ze's Send
#            with the peer's Receive and the mode is Send rather than None.
#            The proof is on the wire: ze prefixes each NLRI with the four-octet
#            Path Identifier RFC 7911 Section 3 defines.
# PREVENTS:  the mirrored direction. ze-peer used to copy ze's OPEN whole, so it
#            answered Send at a Send, the intersection was AddPathNone, and the
#            session negotiated ADD-PATH OFF with no error anywhere. Nothing
#            checked it, so the defect was a coverage hole rather than a failure:
#            no .ci in the tree configured a one-directional ADD-PATH.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: the expected UPDATE carries a Path Identifier. With the
# direction mirrored the negotiation yields None, ze writes the NLRI with no
# identifier, the message is four octets shorter, and the hex below cannot match.
#
# This file also exercises the derived peer AS: it names no option=asn, so the
# AS ze-peer opens with comes from the session > asn > remote leaf below
# (declarePeerAS, internal/test/runner/peer_asn.go).

# ze-peer expectations
stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=timeout:value=15s
# The NLRI carries the RFC 7911 Section 3 Path Identifier (00000000) before the
# prefix 18 0A0000, which is what proves the direction was negotiated.
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF003302000000144001010040020602010000FDE84003040A0001FE00000000180A0000
EOF_PEER

# ze bgp configuration
stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65000
				remote 65001
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
			capability {
				add-path {
					direction send
					family {
						ipv4/unicast
					}
				}
				graceful-restart disable
			}
		}
		behavior {
			group-updates disable
		}

		update {
			attribute {
				origin igp
				next-hop 10.0.1.254
			}
			nlri {
				ipv4/unicast add 10.0.0.0/24
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

# Process orchestration
cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze-peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=15s
